I've queued the fix for #17 again, but it hasn't landed: the build service has no runner to run the gates, so this issue now waits on tacplus-dev/cluster#18.

- **Why the last land was red:** no gate failed. Both build jobs of the change ended with `no verdict within 3h`. Four other repositories doing the same re-pin to tacplus build 2.6.8 (blobstore, tenantecho, coop, pigeon) and looper#109 hit the same timeout. tacplus-dev/build has no runner for its jobs: looper#113 records the symptom, and cluster#18 is the cause. It is the hub's build runner setup, still waiting on Jody's GitLab/GCP steps.
- **The change:** I committed the previous run's work again as 98fabfd on current main (fe44a0a). `go.mod` declares `go 1.27.4`, `build.lock` pins tacplus build 2.6.8 by digest (it has go1.27.4), and README and STATE.md match. It was queued with the manager at 18:11Z on the full gates.
- **Checked locally:** `govulncheck ./...` and `govulncheck -mode binary` on a built binary both print `No vulnerabilities found.` `gofmt` and `go vet` pass, and `looper-trace check` passes with no handlers changed. The govulncheck already installed on this machine can't load a go 1.27 module (looper#109), so I built v1.9.0 with go1.27.4 to run the scans.
- **Not run:** `just gates` in the pinned image, since there is no runner.
- **Release:** no patch is cut from main, because it has a feature since v0.2.0 (#10). The backport, pull request #19 against `release/0.2`, is open, mergeable and green in CI. Tag `v0.2.3` at its merge commit once it merges.

I posted this status on #17 and wrote `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cluster#18` to the run's outcome file, which ends this run. The land stays queued with the manager, so it merges once a runner exists and the gates pass. After that, the next run tags v0.2.3 when #19 merges, posts the final comment and closes #17.
